            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0453" n="443" xml:id="pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.50/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-23T15:00:00-04:00">September 23, 1941—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>262. For the Under Secretary. Referring to my telegram No. 255 of September 18, 5
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">4</hi>] p.m., Dr. Ostria Gutiérrez says he would
                    like to publish the text of his personal message to you in the hope of allaying
                    somewhat criticism to which he continues to be subjected and asked if I thought
                    you would object. I advised him to wait a day or two longer in anticipation of a
                    reply from you and promised in the meantime to inquire whether or not you would
                    consent to the publication of Ostria’s message to you and your answer when it is
                    received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
